'''

for i, (comp, wins) in enumerate(composer_wins.items(), 1):
    html += f'<tr><td>{i}</td><td>{comp}</td><td>{wins}</td></tr>\n'

html += f'''                </tbody>
            </table>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <h2>Temporal Patterns & Decade-by-Decade Breakdown</h2>
            <p>The distribution of wins across decades reveals fascinating patterns: some decades were dominated by a handful of repeat winners while others saw remarkable diversity. The 1990s stand out as the most diverse decade with {decade_unique_winners['1990s']} unique winners, reflecting a period of expansion in the types of films recognized for their scores.</p>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <canvas id="decadeChart"></canvas>
            </div>

            <h3>Decade Breakdown</h3>
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Decade</th><th>Unique Composers</th><th>Total Wins</th><th>Repeat Wins</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
'''

for d in decade_data:
    html += f'<tr><td>{d["decade"]}</td><td>{d["unique_winners"]}</td><td>{d["total_wins"]}</td><td>{d["repeat_wins"]}</td></tr>\n'

html += f'''                </tbody>
            </table>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <h2>Era-Based Analysis of Winning Scores</h2>
            <p>Each era in Oscar history has distinct characteristics that reflect broader industry trends, changing tastes, and the evolution of film music itself.</p>

            <div class="chart-container small">
