                    <h4>Silver Age (1960–1979)</h4>
                    <p>A transitional era that saw the rise of John Barry's elegant simplicity and John Williams' emergence as a force. The period began exploring more diverse instrumentation and stylistic approaches, from Burt Bacharach's pop-inflected scores to the avant-garde sensibilities of Midnight Express.</p>
                </div>
