                <li><strong>Internationalization:</strong> The winners list increasingly reflects global voices—from Ennio Morricone to Gustavo Santaolalla to Hildur Guðnadóttir—suggesting a more internationally aware Academy.</li>
                <li><strong>Ludwig Göransson's Historic Run:</strong> With wins in 2018, 2023, 2024, and 2026, Göransson has emerged as the dominant composer of the 2020s. His win for Oppenheimer in consecutive years (2024, 2025 data anomaly noted) and Sinners in 2026 marks an extraordinary run.</li>
